ing", "inContext": false}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\n# Light green at (30,20), in the dark red block\n# Need to move UP to the blue block/checkerboard at (20,18)-(23,21)\n# Then RIGHT to the yellow block at (20,24)-(21,25)\n\n# From (30,20) to (20,20): UP 10 steps\n# But the blue block is at (20,18)-(23,21), so I need to move UP to row 20\n\n# Let me try moving UP 10 steps to reach the blue block\nresult = action(['UP', 'UP', 'UP', 'UP', 'UP', 'UP', 'UP', 'UP', 'UP', 'UP'])\nprint(f\"After 10 UP: level_completed={last_action_result.get('level_completed')}\")\n\nseg = current_frame.segmentation\nfor n in seg['nodes']:\n    if n['color'] == 'N':\n        boundary = n['boundary']\n        min_row = min(p[0] for p in boundary)\n        min_col = min(p[1] for p in boundary)\n        print(f\"Light green at ({min_row},{min_col})\")\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL RESULT: python", "content": "After 10 UP: level_completed=False\nLight green at (30,20)", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}], "hasExactModelContext": false, "requestIndexWithinTurn": null, "messageCount": 0}, "context": {"sections": [{"label": "USER PROMPT", "content": "The code executed 4 actions in the previous sequence.\nExecuted actions: RIGHT, RIGHT, RIGHT, RIGHT.\nYou are still on the same level.\nCurrent state: step 64, level 1.\nValid actions right now: UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, MOUSE.\nOnly tool: `python`. It receives `current_frame`, `previous_frame`, `history`, `transitions`, `last_transition`, `valid_actions`, `last_action_result`, and `action(actions)`. It also provides `last_animation` (per-action frames of your last `action(...)` call) and `frame_stats` (how much this game has animated so far) -- optional; use them only if you judge the intermediate motion informative rather than incidental.\nOnly letter-coded board views and lightweight metadata are exposed; raw numeric c